WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.501
-Welcome back to the show.
Thanks so much for coming back.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.234
-Thank you for continuously
allowing me to come here.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:07.000
-What do you mean?
We -- We love you here.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.701
There's so much I want
to get into here.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:12.100
But first, I --
I just want to --

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.067
Everything's going on
with you and Justin.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.567
You've had a rough couple
of months.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.667
How is everything going?

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.133
-Everything is good.
I -- I'm doing okay.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.000
My -- my health scare
has, you know --

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.534
We've -- We've moved on from it.
-Yeah, you look good.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:27.601
-And I'm just kind of
allowing my body the time

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:30.767
to heal and do its thing,
but I'm doing okay.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.501
He's also doing okay.
-Okay. Good.

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:35.701
-Obviously, it's been
a weird turn of events

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.367
the last couple months
and the last even few days.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:39.767
-Gotta be scary.
-But he's okay.

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.601
And he's gonna be totally okay.
-Okay. Good.

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
I'm so happy.

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:46.968
Have to -- Have to ask.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:51.234
You have a giant career
and a giant career ahead of you,

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:54.000
but now you finally have
your own skin-care line.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.901
And we were talking about this.
This was years ago.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.200
-Yeah.
-We were discussing this.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.767
-Yeah.
-This -- You know,

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.133
I was looking,
and it's been almost ten years

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:03.300
since you moved to the city
to start modeling.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.234
-Yes.
-And look at you now.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:06.434
But I mean -- But what --

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:08.601
What do you remember
about those days?

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.000
-You know, I moved
into the city when I was --

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.300
I was 17.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.934
I kind of had an agreement
with my parents.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:14.434
I had really
just started modeling

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:15.868
and I was begging them like,

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.334
"Let me move into the city.
Please.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:18.934
It's so much easier
for just everything,

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.601
for travel and for castings."

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.767
And they were like,
"Absolutely not,

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.901
unless you can afford it
on your own."

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.033
And I was like, "Okay, deal.

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.133
If I book a job
where I can afford it,

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:31.033
my own rent for the whole year,
you have to let me move out."

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.667
And I booked my first job,
and it was for the whole year

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.534
of rent, like, to the dollar.

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:37.067
So I was like, "You said..."

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.601
-"You said, so I..."

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:39.901
-So, I moved out, but I --

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:43.234
I lived with my older sister
until I turned 18.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:46.300
But something
that I vividly remember

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:51.133
about moving into the city and
having my first apartment was --

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.734
I was out to dinner
one night with Justin.

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.434
-Yeah.
-And he was like,

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.300
"So you got your own place.
How's it been?"

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.868
Like, "You got
all your furniture?

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.467
You have everything you need?"

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:00.634
And I'm like,
"Yeah, it's amazing.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.200
I love it.
You know, I have a couch.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.200
It's great. I have dishes.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.601
I have spoons."
-It's a big deal.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:06.767
It's a big deal. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.234
-Yeah, like,
everything is such a big deal.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.033
And he's like,
"Well, that's amazing."

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:11.501
Like, "Is there anything
you don't have yet?

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:12.868
Is there anything,
like, you're missing?"

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:14.300
And I'm like, "Yeah,
I don't have a TV yet,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.434
but it's like --
I'm gonna get one.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:16.434
It's, like, not a big deal."

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:18.300
And he was like,
"Okay, okay, cool."

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.067
And then he was driving me home,
and on the way he was like,

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.000
"I can't do this.
We got to go to Best Buy."

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.701
So he took me to Best Buy
on the way home,

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.267
and I was, like,
mortified because I'm like,

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:31.334
"You're not
about to buy me a TV."

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.400
And he bought me a TV.
-No way.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.367
[ Audience awws ]

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:40.167
-And he -- he carried it up --
he carried it upstairs himself.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:41.801
He unboxed it,
did the whole thing.

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:44.000
It was really cute.
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.968
Justin, you're a good man.
You're a gentleman.

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:47.434
-I still have the TV
to this day.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:49.501
-You still have it?
-I still have it to this day.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.000
I could not get rid of the TV,
you guys. It was too cute.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.667
-Yeah, you can't
get rid of it now.

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.467
-No, it's -- it's still
in our apartment to this day.

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:57.434
-Yeah, you have to keep it.
-Yeah.

00:02:57.434 --> 00:03:00.100
-Who -- Who got you
started in fashion?

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.367
Who got you interested?

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.934
Do you -- Was it your mom?
Your sister?

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:05.234
-I mean, I definitely always
looked at my mom's style

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:08.234
and admired it and I felt like
she was always was --

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:10.300
was passionate
about clothing and fashion.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.334
But I would say
I definitely was inspired

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.834
in the modeling space
from the greats --

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.901
Kate Moss, Christy Turlington,
Naomi Campbell.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:22.200
-And then I read somewhere you
named those icons and you said,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.100
"And also Hannah Montana."

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.501
-Um, yeah.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.701
I -- I technically was also
very fashion-inspired

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:34.300
at the time by Hannah Montana,
a.k.a. Miley Cyrus.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.167
She used to wear --
-I mean, that's --

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.467
A lot of people out there
feel the same way.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:40.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Right?!

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:43.367
She used to wear, like,
outfits on "Hannah Montana"

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.133
that I would try to recreate

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.133
because I thought they were
just, like, everything.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:50.000
-Yeah. I never knew that
your middle name was Rhode.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.834
-Yes. It's also
my mom's middle name.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:54.334
-A beautiful name.
R-H-O-D-E. I love that.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:57.534
I go, "Oh, and that is the name
of your new line."

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:58.868
-It is.
-"Rhode."

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.868
Are you -- Today is
officially -- This is real now.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.133
Look at this.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:07.367
-Uh...

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.467
What -- What made you go like,
"I have to do it"?

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.734
I mean, I'm assuming everyone
just asks about your skin-care

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:14.067
routine all the time and --
-Yeah, it definitely was, like,

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.868
the thing I would get
asked about the most,

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:18.000
especially even working
with different makeup artists.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.667
They would always be like,
"What do you do for your skin?"

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:22.767
It was just always something
I felt really passionate about.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.934
I was always someone who is,
and still am,

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:27.901
clearly, to this day,
very committed to a routine,

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:30.868
very regimented person
who is, like, very OCD

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:33.033
about a skin-care routine.

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:36.300
And I just felt like over
the last almost ten years

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.667
of working in this industry,

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:42.234
I felt like I was really able
to develop my beauty philosophy.

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:44.634
And I got to a point
where I was like,

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:48.000
"I want to make a curated,
edited line of essentials,

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.067
like, my go-to things
that can work for everyone."

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:52.834
So the way I --
-Did you always know the name

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.400
"Rhode" was gonna be the title?

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.167
-I wasn't sure
in the very beginning.

00:04:57.167 --> 00:05:01.167
I always knew I wanted "Rhode"
to be a brand that I started.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.801
And as I was developing
and having the conversations

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.767
about the skin-care brand,
"Rhode Skin"

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.667
just kept calling me
and coming to me.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.234
And I also felt like
it was very fitting

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:13.167
because my mom taught me so much
about taking care of myself

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.734
and skin care and sun care
and all these different things.

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:18.968
So I thought there was a really
nice story there with the name.

00:05:18.968 --> 00:05:22.968
-Yeah. I -- I know
you released this as a teaser,

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:25.300
and I want to ask you about this
because I think it's funny.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.834
And there's you
posing with a doughnut.

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.601
[ Laughter ]
-Yes, that is me.

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:32.601
-Yeah, I --
Yeah, a glazed doughnut.

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:34.000
And -- And then I was like,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.467
"Okay, there must be
something to this."

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.033
-Yes.
-Because I was like, "What..."

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:38.501
It's you and
the glazed doughnut.

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:39.801
But it went everywhere.

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:42.534
And then you said that
when you go to bed at night,

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:45.067
you want to feel -- you want
to look like a glazed --

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:47.434
-I want to give off the vibe
of a glazed doughnut.

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:49.133
[ Laughter ]
You know what I mean?

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.234
-Like --
-Edible, dewey,

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:52.634
yummy, delicious.

00:05:52.634 --> 00:05:56.000
-Dewey.
-Glazed.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.601
-I loved that that is your --

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:59.167
that's your thing
you want to do.

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:01.067
[ Applause ]

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:04.067
[ Laughs ] You're also
doing something really cool

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:07.000
that I want to mention called
the Rhode Futures Foundation.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.133
-Yeah, so --
-You're using some of

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:10.968
the proceeds to help women.

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:13.467
-Yes, we are using proceeds
from Rhode to hopefully

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:15.767
in the first year support
and help a thousand women

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:18.033
through three different
amazing organizations.

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:20.133
-See? Come on.
That's how you do it, buddy.

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:22.901
You give back. You work so hard.
Congratulations.

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.767
It's officially out.
-It's officially out.

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:26.467
-I'm so happy you're here.
-Thank you.

00:06:26.467 --> 00:06:28.834
-You look fantastic. Thanks.
Come back whenever you want.

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:31.501
Hailey Bieber, everyone.
Check out her new skin-care line

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:33.400
"Rhode,"
which is available right now.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.367
We'll be right back
with Austin Butler.

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:36.801
Stick around. Come on back.

